## Revision 2 — post-implementation `TEST_CONTRACT_DISPUTE`, arbitration `DISPUTE_UPHELD_TEST_WRONG`

After the Implementer's phase-3 attempt landed `complete`/`delete`/`reopen`'s series-awareness, `npm test` surfaced one failure outside `test/tasks.test.ts`: `test/series.test.ts`'s AC-16 test (`"reads each series with its open occurrence id, or null once it closes; an unknown id is 404"`) asserted `afterCompleteBody.series.openOccurrenceId` was `null` immediately after `POST /api/tasks/:id/complete` closed that series' occurrence. That series (`VALID_SERIES_BODY`) carries no `endKind`/`untilDate`/`maxCount`, so it defaults to `endKind: "never"` (`src/worker/routes/series.ts:106`) and has reached no end condition — meaning AC-19, now implemented, was REQUIRED to spawn a successor for it, which made `openOccurrenceId` the successor's real id, not `null`. The test's own header comment (written in Phase 2, before AC-19 existed) had already flagged this as a Phase-2-only assumption pending Phase 3.

The Implementer raised this as a `TEST_CONTRACT_DISPUTE` rather than silently reinterpreting or weakening the test itself (forbidden by `docs/anti-patterns.md`, restated in this plan's own `## Notes`). `code-reviewer` in arbitration mode (`code-review.jsonl` line 1, 2026-09-24T14:21:02Z) upheld the dispute as `DISPUTE_UPHELD_TEST_WRONG`: AC-16 only promises "their current open occurrence id (or `null`)" and is satisfied either way, so the contradiction was between the test's own hardcoded `null` and AC-19's now-shipped requirement — not a Phase 3 implementation defect. The arbitration verdict independently re-ran `npx vitest run test/series.test.ts test/tasks.test.ts` and confirmed exactly one failure (`test/series.test.ts:265`, expected `null`, received the successor's real id; `test/tasks.test.ts` itself fully green at 24/24) and confirmed via `git status --short` that the Implementer had authored no test-file edit.

Per the arbitration's `proposed_resolution`, the test pair (not the Implementer) amended the disputed test: `test/series.test.ts:259-270` now captures the `complete` response's `successor.id` as `successorId`, asserts it `toBeDefined()`, and asserts `afterCompleteBody.series.openOccurrenceId` equals it instead of asserting `null`; the comment above was rewritten from the "out of scope, Phase 3's concern" note to state the current, shipped reason. This is the Lifecycle ledger's `EXISTING_TEST_UPDATED` row above — anti-weakening holds because the dropped `.toBeNull()` was not a live requirement being silently removed: it was factually superseded (this series can no longer produce `null` here once AC-19 always spawns a successor for it), and the replacement is strictly stronger (it now also proves `GET /api/series/:id` correctly tracks the NEW open row via `findOpenOccurrenceId`, not just that the old one closed).

